{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$M : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0005": "$M$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0007": "$M_i$", "MATH_0008": "$i$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\phi : i \\to i'$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0012": "$M(\\phi) : M_i \\to M_{i'}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:912e4b40cd9d749d3414b0677c23c16ab52233d2991306395393952f0b598abd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:158b52cd16c8cc8f310f449f6c21011963c1133325dc8c917cb8682585550d09", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>diagram<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> in <MATH_0002> is\nsimply a functor <MATH_0003>. We say that\n<MATH_0004> is the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>index category<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> or that <MATH_0005> is an\n<MATH_0006>-diagram. We will use the notation <MATH_0007> to denote the\nimage of the object\n<MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009>. Hence for <MATH_0010> a morphism\nin <MATH_0011> we have <MATH_0012>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:951d126f0af7c151b6c2fb5588c9018f5ff6e119340949eb478efa25c688569f", "unit_id": "tag:002D:paragraph-0001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0002": "$M$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\lim_\\mathcal{I} M$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$p_i : \\lim_\\mathcal{I} M \\to M_i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\phi : i \\to i'$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0009": "$p_{i'} = M(\\phi) \\circ p_i$", "MATH_0010": "$W$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0012": "$q_i : W \\to M_i$", "MATH_0013": "$i \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{I})$", "MATH_0014": "$\\phi : i \\to i'$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0016": "$q_{i'} = M(\\phi) \\circ q_i$", "MATH_0017": "$q : W \\to \\lim_\\mathcal{I} M$", "MATH_0018": "$q_i = p_i \\circ q$", "MATH_0019": "$i$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-limit}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4450b79feb640edeb5aded763db826721bfca04e8c1d434610616a12712cfda7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1426156aa629b3f3765a54ae19cfb8d8d09aba17a677c8f4731c8488a1a861df", "source_text": "A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>limit<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of the <MATH_0001>-diagram <MATH_0002> in the category\n<MATH_0003> is given by an object <MATH_0004> in <MATH_0005>\ntogether with morphisms <MATH_0006> such that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> for <MATH_0007> a morphism\nin <MATH_0008> we have <MATH_0009>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> for any object <MATH_0010> in <MATH_0011> and any family of\nmorphisms <MATH_0012> (indexed by <MATH_0013>)\nsuch that for all <MATH_0014>\nin <MATH_0015> we have <MATH_0016> there\nexists a unique morphism <MATH_0017> such that\n<MATH_0018> for every object <MATH_0019> of <MATH_0020>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a122b6ef7cba054c4ea8304a21d8af4d23d5fe0eadc89ca2cf482f92933bb5f8", "unit_id": "tag:002E:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\lim_\\mathcal{I} M, (p_i)_{i\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{I})})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ad9e5d50477ae3cc6ef20f147351e963100249c9dd02f64c3a66dfcdbaa7bd1a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6af5c02c3803d755d4838ac6ee5e90d1a565a480dc097c53703717d917ca9e8f", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nLimits <MATH_0001> are\n(if they exist)\nunique up to unique isomorphism by the uniqueness requirement\nin the definition. Products of pairs, fibre products, and equalizers are\nexamples of limits. The limit over the empty diagram is a final object\nof <MATH_0002>.\nIn the category of sets all limits exist.\nThe dual notion is that of colimits.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3e991771737f394541a3aff1f5136aa5c02622e28f863a6c92d10a708737e50d", "unit_id": "tag:002D:paragraph-0002"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0002": "$M$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\colim_\\mathcal{I} M$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$s_i : M_i \\to \\colim_\\mathcal{I} M$", "MATH_0007": "$\\phi : i \\to i'$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0009": "$s_i = s_{i'} \\circ M(\\phi)$", "MATH_0010": "$W$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0012": "$t_i : M_i \\to W$", "MATH_0013": "$i \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{I})$", "MATH_0014": "$\\phi : i \\to i'$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0016": "$t_i = t_{i'} \\circ M(\\phi)$", "MATH_0017": "$t : \\colim_\\mathcal{I} M \\to W$", "MATH_0018": "$t_i = t \\circ s_i$", "MATH_0019": "$i$", "MATH_0020": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-colimit}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a7c8012fb726f212d54ea8f93819ee845bac3276adb99bfad62d398f93f0820d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:759316fc302e9c418d92bbc1db81d148683784a7a8bc418c3ec6285671f9f11e", "source_text": "A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>colimit<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of the <MATH_0001>-diagram <MATH_0002> in the category\n<MATH_0003> is given by an object <MATH_0004> in <MATH_0005>\ntogether with morphisms <MATH_0006> such that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> for <MATH_0007> a morphism\nin <MATH_0008> we have <MATH_0009>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> for any object <MATH_0010> in <MATH_0011> and any family of\nmorphisms <MATH_0012> (indexed by <MATH_0013>)\nsuch that for all <MATH_0014>\nin <MATH_0015> we have <MATH_0016> there\nexists a unique morphism <MATH_0017> such that\n<MATH_0018> for every object <MATH_0019> of <MATH_0020>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2ce18f4c2f79ddbb49877455634d922ff2c9119f862e2a12c9f19f82d12c43f7", "unit_id": "tag:002F:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\colim_\\mathcal{I} M, (s_i)_{i\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{I})})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e0f91663095dec67800d5a24a97428dd79d9ba2fd9636b2a768eee3ab0e0ac32", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aadfc44f45f08264e2bf995fca0c4980bbfeb429e414373b7aa26149e0d79673", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nColimits <MATH_0001> are\n(if they exist) unique up to unique isomorphism by the uniqueness requirement\nin the definition. Coproducts of pairs, pushouts, and coequalizers are\nexamples of colimits. The colimit over an empty diagram is an initial object\nof <MATH_0002>. In the category of sets all colimits exist.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1b18689b5b51c1c4cc2d2e8552a16bb10f70af78c95023bc17be64a4bc3b7f5a", "unit_id": "tag:002D:paragraph-0003"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-big-categories}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-diagram-small}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f95d4ee2af62a80c081971d95c29778dd16768e008bb6fc6ee45764fc75483f4", "source_text": "The index category of a (co)limit will never be allowed to have\na proper class of objects. In this project it means that\nit cannot be one of the categories listed in\nRemark <REF_0001>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9e1d095f4d1aaae3e5ecf42576863b570ca4782ea75e3bab80a75bcb2d95b114", "unit_id": "tag:002G:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\lim_i M_i$", "MATH_0002": "$\\colim_i M_i$", "MATH_0003": "$\\lim_{i\\in \\mathcal{I}} M_i$", "MATH_0004": "$\\colim_{i\\in \\mathcal{I}} M_i$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0006": "$M : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\lim_i M_i$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(W, \\lim_i M_i)\n=\n\\lim_i \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(W, M_i)\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$\\colim_i M_i$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(\\colim_i M_i, W)\n=\n\\lim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}^{opp}} \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(M_i, W)\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-limit-sets}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-limit-colim}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cad7bcd3f1eeeceec6de639aa8b493bcecf9276eb93759758a040928b88d8129", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:92b4eaf9cc172050774fd682d1b52e06dd94ec0901d807743701ef9ea53d83e8", "source_text": "We often write <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002>,\n<MATH_0003>, or <MATH_0004>\ninstead of the versions indexed by <MATH_0005>.\nUsing this notation, and using the description of\nlimits and colimits of sets in Section <REF_0001>\nbelow, we can say the following.\nLet <MATH_0006> be a diagram.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The object <MATH_0007> if it exists satisfies the following property\n<MATH_0008>\nwhere the limit on the right takes place in the category of sets.\n<STRUCT_0003> The object <MATH_0009> if it\nexists satisfies the following property\n<MATH_0010>\nwhere on the right we have the limit over the opposite category\nwith value in the category of sets.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nBy the Yoneda lemma (and its dual) this formula completely determines the\nlimit, respectively the colimit.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:51d40cfd0fb77378565a8d9d801da9475eb0c793eea4a5ec5dee1cfe7321b7e1", "unit_id": "tag:002H:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$I$", "MATH_0002": "$i \\in I$", "MATH_0003": "$M_i$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\prod_{i\\in I} M_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\lim_\\mathcal{I} M$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0008": "$I$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-product}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:617f66816e5dc3ef2ec9a46ac298f924b237e71af1386c7d6b70bd958ea65f31", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:61d719b4c9ba62504ebf5df0d64c931cd021e3a90b22120a69ea487408b86e5c", "source_text": "Suppose that <MATH_0001> is a set, and suppose given for every <MATH_0002> an\nobject <MATH_0003> of the category <MATH_0004>. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>product<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\n<MATH_0005> is by definition <MATH_0006>\n(if it exists)\nwhere <MATH_0007> is the category having only identities as\nmorphisms and having the elements of <MATH_0008> as objects.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cba7300e16e2a1f6ddd31681bad47a0d44967b8e7bb8763166d1fe40311f728b", "unit_id": "tag:002I:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$I = \\emptyset$", "MATH_0002": "$p_i : \\prod M_i \\to M_i$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b4b3102c1002a85313d7f1fc5ec5795dfd6f28e00d6bfc7e975477ed9f95e62d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1920168f93ac696926f5ac7aea40c4cca71d21d00fce7a7ca7154217cd22cf4b", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nAn important special case is where <MATH_0001> in which case the\nproduct is a final object of the category.\nThe morphisms <MATH_0002> are called the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>projection morphisms<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:582538f5b3dfb3543b3fa62257e6d5ded480c246ef80f82aeb241235a48715b5", "unit_id": "tag:002D:paragraph-0005"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$I$", "MATH_0002": "$i \\in I$", "MATH_0003": "$M_i$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\coprod_{i\\in I} M_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\colim_\\mathcal{I} M$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0008": "$I$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-coproduct}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b66256fb44156357a236b94e9f5021a3f8ebef039eef1226467e5e6382cd278", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bd8320b90e0572439724fb286d7f12a71ec022fec55a9ead7f29bd0b9502fd01", "source_text": "Suppose that <MATH_0001> is a set, and suppose given for every <MATH_0002> an\nobject <MATH_0003> of the category <MATH_0004>. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>coproduct<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\n<MATH_0005> is by definition <MATH_0006>\n(if it exists) where <MATH_0007> is the category having only\nidentities as morphisms and having the elements of <MATH_0008> as objects.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:acb9816b68a63e3eb4965ad4fffb0c824c27d72d96269bd70d901966ab67a751", "unit_id": "tag:002J:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "002D", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$I = \\emptyset$", "MATH_0002": "$M_i \\to \\coprod M_i$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8c93d6de64bf0dcfb2a4cd4efd8ac1d11cccee3ccc971fd910f35bcb665d9f95", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ffb6851c113dab266363b98e3a3528f055cc2a0a7e9f52168a29a3163e63f381", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nAn important special case is where <MATH_0001> in which case the\ncoproduct is an initial object of the category.\nNote that the coproduct comes equipped with morphisms\n<MATH_0002>. These are sometimes called the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>coprojections<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:65822dee51e6a66708302b99e12750dec7c93f45e9fd5f613baf09d3a46362c4", "unit_id": "tag:002D:paragraph-0006"}
